        "date": "2026-11-08T03:53:06Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): machine files for the other Tormach mills; belt ranges and rigid tapping from the .mch\n\nShips inch machine files for the Tormach 770MX (ML), 770M, 1100MX,\n1500MX and PCNC 440, each from its own Tormach operator's manual\n(UM10864, UM10539, UM10586, UM10811, UM10372), next to the 770MX (MF,\nUM10587) from #131.\n\nThe .mch spindle gains two optional fields:\n- `ranges` (the hand-changed belt ranges), read by the Tormach post's\n  belt note as `machine.spindleRanges` in place of the 770 family's\n  hard-coded numbers. A one-range machine gets no note.\n- `rigid_tapping`, which the post reads as `machine.rigidTapping`. It\n  is false on the R8 mills (770M, PCNC 440), where the post refuses a\n  tap cycle by name instead of writing G84.\n\nUnstated, both read as before for every other machine. The generic-VMC\nsynth golden loses its 770-family belt comment.\n\nNot shipped: the non-MX 1100 and the plain 770 (no manual in hand).\n\nRefs #170\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
